  "definition": {
    "scope": "Every number is counted from the live rows in this system's database. In this demo those rows include records made by the seed script and by simulated-clock runs, so the figures describe this deployment, not AICTE's real caseload.",
    "events": "Number of audit-log events matching the filters (From/To on the event time, inclusive; actor = the role that acted; action; entity). Each event is counted once in each of byActorRole, byAction and byEntity, so each breakdown adds up to total. Entity: APPLICATION = an event on a case, RULE_PACK = a rule-pack change, SYSTEM = anything else (sign-ins, clock changes, demo resets). Only counts are returned; no case content is exposed here.",
    "integrity": "Recomputed now over the WHOLE audit log, not just the filtered events: each chain's hashes are re-derived and compared with the stored links, so an edited event or a broken link in a chain is reported. ok = no chain failed. It reports damage after the fact; it does not prevent anyone with database access from changing rows."
  },
